# FPGA Edge AI Image Enhancement
> A full FPGA-oriented image enhancement pipeline using Residual CNNs, INT8 quantization, and Xilinx Vitis AI for real-time edge inference.
---
## Overview
Most image enhancement systems stop at GPU inference:
```python
model(image)

This project does the opposite — the entire pipeline is designed around FPGA deployment, low-latency inference, and hardware-aware optimization.

From Quantization-Aware Training (QAT) to Vitis AI compilation and DPU execution, every stage is implemented with embedded Edge AI deployment in mind.

The result is a real-time FPGA image enhancement system capable of:

* low-light restoration
* denoising
* blur reduction
* efficient INT8 inference
* hardware-accelerated deployment

⸻

Features

Component	Implementation
Deep Learning Model	Residual CNN architecture
Quantization	INT8 Quantization-Aware Training
FPGA Workflow	Xilinx Vitis AI deployment
Hardware Acceleration	DPU inference engine
Enhancement Tasks	Denoising, low-light enhancement, deblurring
Evaluation	PSNR and SSIM metrics
Deployment	Docker-based runtime
Target Platform	FPGA Edge AI systems

No TensorRT. No GPU dependency during deployment. Built specifically for FPGA acceleration pipelines.

⸻

Project Structure

FPGA-Image-Enhancement/
│
├── models/                  # Trained and quantized models
├── testing_code/            # Inference and evaluation scripts
├── testing_images/          # Sample input images
├── output/                  # Enhanced output images
├── results/                 # Benchmark and evaluation outputs
├── docs/                    # Technical documentation
│
├── Dockerfile
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md

⸻

Quick Start

Option 1 — Docker (Recommended)

Docker provides a reproducible FPGA inference environment.

# Build Docker image
docker build -t fpga-enhancement .
# Run container
docker run -it fpga-enhancement

⸻

Option 2 — Manual Installation

Requirements: Python 3.10+, PyTorch, Vitis AI Runtime

⸻

Step 1 — Clone Repository

git clone https://github.com/your-username/FPGA-Image-Enhancement.git
cd FPGA-Image-Enhancement

⸻

Step 2 — Install Dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

⸻

Step 3 — Run Inference

python testing_code/test.py

⸻

System Pipeline

Input Image
    │
    ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Residual CNN Train  │  Learn enhancement mappings using residual blocks
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Quantization Aware  │  Simulate INT8 arithmetic during training
│ Training (QAT)      │
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ INT8 Optimization   │  Reduce precision for FPGA efficiency
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Vitis AI Compiler   │  Compile network for DPU execution
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ XModel Generation   │  Generate deployable FPGA artifact
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ DPU FPGA Inference  │  Hardware-accelerated CNN execution
└─────────┬───────────┘
          │
          ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│ Enhanced Output     │  Restored and denoised image output
└─────────────────────┘

⸻

Technical Reference

Residual CNN Architecture

* Residual learning improves convergence stability
* Preserves low-frequency image information
* Enables deeper enhancement networks with reduced degradation

Quantization-Aware Training (QAT)

* Simulates INT8 inference during training
* Minimizes accuracy loss after quantization
* Produces FPGA-ready deployment models

INT8 Optimization

* Converts FP32 operations into fixed-point arithmetic
* Reduces memory and compute overhead
* Improves DPU inference efficiency

Vitis AI Deployment

* Model compiled using Xilinx Vitis AI toolchain
* Generates .xmodel FPGA deployment artifacts
* Targets DPU hardware accelerators

DPU Hardware Acceleration

* Offloads CNN inference from CPU to FPGA fabric
* Enables low-latency real-time execution
* Improves throughput and power efficiency

Evaluation Metrics

* PSNR — reconstruction quality measurement
* SSIM — perceptual image similarity metric

⸻

Performance

Metric	CPU	FPGA
Precision	FP32	INT8
Inference Speed	0.85 – 1.3 FPS	8.37 FPS
Deployment Target	CPU	FPGA DPU
Relative Performance	1×	8–10× Faster

The FPGA implementation significantly improves throughput while maintaining stable enhancement quality under INT8 quantization.

⸻

FPGA Deployment Workflow

PyTorch Model
      ↓
Quantization
      ↓
Vitis AI Compilation
      ↓
.xmodel Generation
      ↓
DPU Deployment
      ↓
FPGA Inference

Deployment artifact:

models/model_b8_c128_int.xmodel

